# Tritonian Sea Wolf

## Lore

The Sea Wolves are a combination of troubleshooter, security officer, underwater combat specialist and marine soldier. Born in Tritonia''s floating habitat, they are volunteers who show a natural talent for dealing with danger, and are trained from their teens in combat, counter-intelligence and the hazards of the sea.

Many are injured or killed in the line of duty, and they neither regret nor resent it: the whole colony is in danger from outside, and they at least have the honour of doing something about it. It is also why nearly half of them carry cybernetic prosthetics or bio-implants in place of lost limbs, eyes and organs.

## GM Notes

Typical Sea Wolf missions cover Tritonia''s security, underwater rescue, commando operations and counter-terrorism, and the role of sea scout, city patrolman and soldier hunting down threats to the colony. As the artificial island''s defence force they gather and use intelligence, maintain the law, keep the peace and work as police officers.

They also run deep-sea investigations and salvage - looking into underwater anomalies, alien habitats, vessels and wreckage, and searching wrecks and ruins for anything valuable.

Amphibs often join the Sea Wolves; they make excellent underwater scouts and explorers.
', 'published', 'data-script'
